| design | stage 01 | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. Load the gene counts matrix and design table using Python in the gars-bio environment.
2. Filter genes with low counts (keep genes with rowMeans > 1 count per million equivalent).
3. Normalize counts using TMM (trimmed mean of M-values) normalization via edgeR functions in R.
4. Apply log2 transformation (log2(counts + 1)).
5. Compute principal component analysis (PCA) on the normalized log-transformed counts using scikit-learn's PCA.
6. Generate a scatter plot of PC1 vs PC2, coloring points by the condition column (untreated=blue, treated=red). Include sample IDs as labels. Add a legend and title.
7. Save the plot as a PNG file with 300 dpi resolution.

